# Give the player several followers standing together, then change level, so
# INCURSION_FOLLOWER_PROBE can report whether every follower came along.
#
#   INCURSION_FOLLOWER_PROBE=1 tools/headless.sh tools/keys/followers.keys 3362
#
# Why several, and why together: the collection loop in Player::MoveDepth walks
# m->Things by index and removes as it goes. Array::Remove shifts the tail
# left, so the entry that slides into the index just vacated is never examined.
# A single follower therefore always survives. The defect needs two followers
# adjacent in Things, which is what summoning several in a row produces --
# creatures are appended to Things in creation order.
#
# Wizard menu letters are positional (src/TextTerm.cpp:941):
#   g = Monster Summoning              (7th option)
#   p = Ascend / Descend Depth         (16th option)
#   C = Make Player Master of Monster  (29th option)
# and inside Monster Summoning: [J] Kobolds, then [c] kobold. Wizard mode asks
# for a confirmation the first time only, which is the 'y' below.
#
# The wizard summon does NOT make the monster a companion -- that only happens
# on the spell and wand path (src/Encounter.cpp:2511) -- so each kobold is made
# a follower afterwards with the master command.

@include chargen.keys

w y g J c l UP ENTER
w g J c l UP ENTER
w g J c l UP ENTER

@dump:summoned

w C UP ENTER
w C UP LEFT ENTER
w C RIGHT ENTER

@dump:mastered

w p "2" ENTER

@dump:descended
